The Calyx Public Open Source License 1.0 ("CPOSL-1.0" or "License") governs the
use, reproduction, modification, and distribution of the Calyx Quantum Proof
Encryption Protocol ("Calyx QPEP" / "OpenQPEP"), the Quantum Proof Key Ring File
(".qpkrf") specification, and associated reference software created by Tristen
Martinez at Calyx Labs Inc.

1. DEFINITIONS
--------------
1.1 "Protocol Standard" means the Calyx Quantum Proof Encryption Protocol
    (Calyx QPEP), including its QLX-768, QLX-1024, and QLX-2048 lattice key
    encapsulation tiers, HGC-448 birational curve combiner, QVS-65, QVS-87, and
    QVS-128 vector signature schemes, qSponge-512 cryptographic transcript
    sponge, Calyx-Cascade-512 (CC-512) dual-stream authenticated matrix cipher,
    QPKD-Argon memory-hard passphrase derivation lock, and the .qpkrf key ring
    file format.
1.2 "Licensor" means Calyx Labs Inc. and original creator Tristen Martinez.
1.3 "Covered Work" means the Original Work of authorship or any Derivative Work
    thereof distributed under this License.

