Source Code and Object Form.

3. MANDATORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC INTEGRITY & PASSPHRASE ENFORCEMENT CONDITION
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
To prevent cryptographic downgrade attacks and protect end-user security across
the Calyx QPEP ecosystem, any Covered Work or Derivative Work that reads,
writes, generates, or claims interoperability with Calyx QPEP packets or .qpkrf
(Quantum Proof Key Ring File) files MUST strictly preserve:
  (a) The non-bypassable QPKD-Argon Passphrase Policy requiring every passphrase
      to be at least twelve (12) characters in length and contain at least two
      (2) numeric digits, four (4) special characters, two (2) uppercase
      letters, and four (4) lowercase letters;
  (b) The atomic .qpkrf self-certification verification checks; and
  (c) The dual-stream CC-512 authenticated frame integrity verification.

Derivative Works that strip or weaken these security guarantees MUST NOT use the
names "Calyx QPEP", "OpenQPEP", or the ".qpkrf" file extension.

